1
00:00:08,860 --> 00:00:14,892
A contract starts as a template, so the
wording is decided once rather than each

2
00:00:14,892 --> 00:00:15,269
time.

3
00:00:15,725 --> 00:00:21,242
It becomes a real contract the moment
somebody accepts an invitation — filled in

4
00:00:21,242 --> 00:00:24,967
with their name, their job
title and their start date.

5
00:00:25,422 --> 00:00:31,181
Who signs, and in what order, is part of
the document rather than an email thread.

6
00:00:31,635 --> 00:00:37,850
Whether it is signed, merely confirmed as
read, or has to be done on paper is part

7
00:00:37,850 --> 00:00:42,548
of the template — not a
decision somebody makes in the moment.

8
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:49,876
And the register says where every
document got to: issued, not opened yet, waiting

9
00:00:49,876 --> 00:00:52,056
on a signature, or signed.

10
00:00:52,514 --> 00:00:57,204
Next: the documents that run
out, and being told before they do.

